## Shipping

Publishing defaults to Reliant hosting (staging/prod are already bound to it): load `deploy`, then `{{.CLI}} env deploy <env>`. One hosted static site per org is free (1 GiB storage cap), counted across environments: each env's deployed site is one. Anything beyond it — a second env's site, any hosted workload or managed database — needs billing, and until billing is set up the deploy is queued, not refused: `env deploy` exits 7 and prints the billing link. Give the user that link; don't retry. Never ask for `forge login` when running under Reliant.

**No Reliant account** (standalone forge, nothing signed in)? `{{.CLI}} env deploy <env> --claimable` publishes with no signup and prints a live URL plus a **claim link**: hand the link to your user (it expires in 72h; opening it signs them up free and makes the deploy theirs, so treat it like a password). It fits one static site, or one service with one database, and is refused when you are signed in. Exit 4 `claimable_throttled` is a rate limit: wait the printed retry-after (never loop), or `forge login`. Depth: `deploy/hosting`.

